aft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100563","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100563","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100563.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100563.patch","merged_at":"2024-12-20T02:11:18Z"},"body":"We've recently begun to introduce move semantics to core, for its performance benefits. Examples of functions that can benefit a lot from move semantics include SWAP (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100367), reduce_at and insert (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100477), and simple data transfer. For more information on motivation, see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100426.\r\n\r\nFor `List`, this is especially important because a copy-constructor and copy-assignment are forced to copy the entire array, and all elements in it. And worse, because `List` is not contiguous, this is slow.\r\n\r\nI first wanted to do a use-case analysis like in #100560, but quickly gave up because there were just too many beneficiaries of `List` move semantics.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"